+# Node-local model cache (design notes)
+
+This directory describes a simple node-local caching approach for model artifacts to reduce cold-starts and NVMe prefetching.
+
+Design:
+- A sidecar or DaemonSet warms the local disk by fetching model shards from the object store (S3/GCS) into /var/local/models/<model>.
+- A small LRU eviction policy keeps disk usage under limit; eviction triggered on disk pressure or age.
+- The model-serving container mounts the node-local path as read-only and loads models from it.
+
+Operations:
+- Configure your PVC or hostPath for the cache area with fast NVMe or local SSD.
+- Ensure sidecar has permissions to fetch artifacts and cosign-verify any artifact metadata before caching.
+
